---
// /brick-choir/third-shot — THIRD SHOT, the phone-native pickleball game: one finger, portrait, deeply strategic. The
// camera sits high behind your baseline so the whole court (and the far kitchen) is on screen; your Buddy (the same
// 14-char code as Pickle Park, localStorage bcp:buddy) plays doubles with a bot partner against two bots with a style
// (bangers, dinkers, lobbers) and a tier (Park, Club, Pro). Your finger is the paddle: a swipe's direction aims, its speed
// is pace, its shape is the shot — a short soft flick dinks (or drops from deep), flat and fast drives, long and up lobs,
// a quick jab at the line speeds it up, a reverse flick resets. The strategy engine (third-engine.js) knows the game:
// net height by x, the attackability rule (below the net = don't attack), the two-bounce rule, the kitchen (volleys,
// momentum, the Erne, the ATP), the third-shot drop, the transition zone, pop-ups that come with patience, and side-out
// scoring with a sung call. Coach callouts, a Shot Report with a Strategy IQ, drills, a seeded daily challenge, a share
// card and /api/brick-scores as game "third". Audio: synthesized paddle pops, bounces, net cord, squeaks, a crowd that
// swells, and the Pickle Park steel-pan/marimba rally music. three.js 0.170 (jsDelivr). Built 2026-09-24 by Claude (Fable).
